# Environment Configuration Example
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored, loaded in all modes) and fill in any
# secrets. The committed `.env.development` / `.env.production` hold the non-secret
# defaults; `.env.local` overrides `.env` but is itself overridden by the per-mode
# files — so only put here what the mode files do NOT already set (e.g. the LLM key).

# LLM (OpenAI-compatible) for the dev-mode NL->intent translation in the Cmd-K
# palette. The KEY is compiled into the browser bundle (VITE_), so use only a
# dev/research key, never a secret production key. The URI + model already have
# committed defaults; you normally only set the key here.
VITE_LLM_API_KEY=your-dev-key-here
# VITE_LLM_API_URI=https://hub.nhr.fau.de/api/llmgw/v1
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8

# The eval (`deno task eval:intent`) reads the SAME file; it accepts either the
# VITE_LLM_* names above or the un-prefixed LLM_* aliases (LLM_API_KEY, ...).
